-- Core retire events, relative to the middle's scope (TOP.NzeaCore.core.middle).
--
-- These are the events the retire counters cannot answer: the counters say how many, these say when and in what order.
-- The stage-side events (issue, operand wait) live beside this file, `issue.pulse`; bind both when the question spans
-- the read and the commit:
--   pulse property --event nzea_core/src/middle/retire.pulse <MIDDLE> Core \
--       --eval 'Core.commit_fire || Core.redirect' --cycles 0-500

-- One instruction retired: register write-back, CSR write and the commit trace all ride this pulse.
commit_fire = commit_valid

-- A mispredicted branch: the write-back register's resolved `next_pc` disagrees with the prediction it was fetched
-- under (`wb_is_branch & next_pc =/= pred_next_pc`, the test `flushing` starts from), so the middle flushes the younger
-- stages and the front restarts from `wb_next_pc`.
redirect = flushing
